view-if: anti_socialist_coalition_r >= 50 and pnf_seating_disp > ul_seating_disp + ldr_seating_disp and (prime_minister_party != "PNF" or prime_minister = "D'Annunzio")
go-to: dannunzio_power if prime_minister = "D'Annunzio"

It seems our <span style="color: [+ communist_colour +];">radicalism</span> and abstentionism has pushed the LDR and UL to ally with the PNF, as a junior partner to their list. [+ pnf_leader +] has made himself crucial to this coalition, and been able to come out on top in the inter-party struggle, being appointed Prime Minister by the <span style="color: [+ i_colour +];">**King**</span>.

- @pnf_prime_minister: What now?

@dannunzio_power

The PNF, under the leadership of Gabriele D'Annunzio, is able to form a coalition, keeping himself as Prime Minister in a majority coalition.

What now?

- @civil_war: We cannot wait any longer. Mobilise the Red Guard!
- @nothing_dannunzio: Bide our time further.

@nothing_dannunzio
subtitle: This will end the game.

[+ pnf_leader +] acts fast, consolidating <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> into a corporative state and empowering the PNF and D'Annunzio into effective dictators of <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> for the foresseable future.

<span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**a**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**ly**</span> is lost.

- @game_over: Game over.

@grand_coalition_yes
subtitle: [? if participating = 1 : This is extremely unpopular with the Reformist faction. ?]
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.participating == 1) {
    Q.reformist_dissent += 15;
}
Q.psi_in_government = 0; 
if (Q.year == 1919) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Nitti"; 
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ldr_name;
} 
if (Q.year == 1920 || Q.year == 1921) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Giolitti";
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ul_name;
}
if (Q.year == 1921) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Bonomi";
    Q.prime_minister_party = "PSRI";
}
if (Q.year > 1921) {
    Q.prime_minister = "Orlando";
    Q.prime_minister_party = Q.ldr_name;
}
Q.interior_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
Q.foreign_minister_party = "UL"; 
Q.justice_minister_party = "I"; 
Q.treasury_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.finance_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.public_works_minister_party = Q.ds_name; 
Q.public_education_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.agriculture_minister_party = "LDR"; 
Q.labour_minister_party = "UL";
!}

Though tense negotiations between the <span style="color: [+ ldr_colour +];">Liberals</span> and newly formed <span style="color: [+ ppi_colour +];">Catholic</span> parties, the coalition of the PPI, [+ ldr_name +], [+ ul_name +] and [+ ds_name +] is established.

@turati
title: Filippo Turati for Prime Minister
subtitle: Turati leads the Reformist wing, and is an acceptable candidate for Prime Minister.
choose-if: reformists_defect = 0
unavailable-subtitle: Turati is no longer a member of the [+ psi_name +].
on-arrival: psi_in_government = 1; prime_minister = "Turati"; prime_minister_party = psi_name;
go-to: ministries

Filippo Turati's appointment as Prime Minister is approved by all our potential allies.

@bissolati
