on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; maximalist_dissent += 5; communist_dissent += 10; ppi_relation += 10; prime_minister = "De Gasperi"; prime_minister_party = "PPI"; psi_in_government = 1; leverage += 5
go-to: ministries

This is highly unexpected, and many in the centre and even the Reformist faction of our party is criticizing this decision.

@liberal_demands
go-to: l_demands_menu

Having met with representatives from the [+ ldr_name +], they have put forward a series of demands we are to either complete or policies we cannot change while in power.
While it seems do have a bit of wiggle room to negotiate, we certainly cannot outright refuse them. What do we do?

**We will have one year to complete the crackdown of violence if given to us.**

Some major ones include: Land Reform, Streetfighting Crackdowns, and Nationalisations,

While some minor ones are: Budget Surplus, Foreign Affairs and Soviet Aid.

@l_demands_menu

- #libdem_major
- #libdem_minor
- @refuse_libdem
- @finalise_libdem
- #drop_libdem_major
- #drop_libdem_minor

@liberal_reform
title: End our violent seizure of land in the South and reject any form of land reform.
subtitle: This will be a major setback if we are to solve the Southern Question anytime soon.
tags: libdem_major
view-if: liberal_reform_accepted = 0
on-arrival: liberal_reform_accepted = 1; liberal_negotiations += 20;
go-to: l_demands_menu

This is a major point of conjecture for the LDR and UL, and secures us significant progress in negotiations.

@liberal_crackdown
title: Begin a crack down of violence in the streets, including the Red Guard.
